Likutay Halachos &middot; Orach Chaim

Hilchos Yom Tov

The Matter of Shabbas and Yom Tov

Halacha 1

The 39 melachos come from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil; Yom Tov = nullification of the evil = they are forbidden. And Rosh HaShanah is a Yom Tov because it commemorates the first day when light and darkness served together &mdash; the moment closest to &ldquo;before the Creation,&rdquo; when the Tachlis illuminated directly.

The Ain Sof: entirely good, &ldquo;Hashem is HaElokim&rdquo;

&darr;

Shabbas = the Tachlis itself = holy of its own accord = above time

&darr; ratzo vashov

Yom Tov = drawing that illumination into y&rsquo;shus (the days)

&darr;

Yisrael sanctify it: mikrah kodesh = call the holiness into time

&darr;

Ochel nefesh permitted (the soul > Yom Tov) / Hazmanah needed (expel S.A.)

&darr;

&ldquo;Yom Tov&rdquo; = a good day: the light of &ldquo;entirely good&rdquo; drawn into the fabric of time

&#10042; Na Nach Nachma Nachman MayUman &#10042;
